edia"},{"animation":false,"id":327,"name":"Takara Tomy"}],"synopsis":{"language":null,"source":"anilist","spoiler":false,"text":"Despite the title, this is not a feature but the three-part OAV Battle Skipper (1995), which Takashi Watanabe directed before going on to Slayers.\n\nWhen the members of the Etiquette Club at St. Ignacio's School for Girls go down the tubes--literally--they acquire the skimpy outfits they wear to pilot the unfortunately named BSs or Battle Skippers, state-of-the-art military mecha. As \"Extars,\" the Etiquette Club members fight to eliminate evil from the world, which means the bizarre schemes of Sayaka, the nasty, super-rich president of the rival Debutante Club, and her flunky, Todo.\n\nThe series was created to promote a line of robot toys from Tomy, and viewers who are willing to accept high school girls' quarrels escalating into battles involving satellite weaponry may enjoy these silly adventures.\n\n(Source: AniDB)"},"tags":[{"name":"Ojou-sama","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"School","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Boarding School","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Ensemble Cast","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Super Robot","rank":70,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Primarily Female Cast","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"School Club","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Female Protagonist","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Military","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Primarily Teen Cast","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Urban","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Henshin","rank":46,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Tanks","rank":46,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Nun","rank":40,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Guns","rank":40,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Unrequited Love","rank":40,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Rape","rank":20,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Nudity","rank":20,"spoiler":false}],"titles":{"display":"BATTLE SKIPPER THE MOVIE","english":"BATTLE SKIPPER THE MOVIE","native":"美少女遊撃隊バトルスキッパー","romaji":"Bishoujo Yuugekitai Battle Skipper","synony